------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Daymet data in the test fixtures
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

tests/fixtures/daymet.ornl.gov/*.json are small extracts of Daymet V4 R1 daily data
(single pixels for 2020, a 3x3 cell mosaic around the EEMT sample DEM, a 2-day window),
fetched on 2026-11-15 without credentials from the ORNL DAAC single-pixel API
(https://daymet.ornl.gov/single-pixel/api/data). tests/fixtures/cmr.earthdata.nasa.gov
holds shrunk NASA CMR granule metadata; tests/fixtures/{opendap,urs}.earthdata.nasa.gov
hold the headers of the unauthenticated Earthdata Login redirect chain.

Daymet data are NOT covered by the MIT License. Cite them as:

  Thornton, M.M., R. Shrestha, Y. Wei, P.E. Thornton, and S-C. Kao. 2022. Daymet: Daily
  Surface Weather Data on a 1-km Grid for North America, Version 4 R1. ORNL DAAC, Oak
  Ridge, Tennessee, USA. https://doi.org/10.3334/ORNLDAAC/2129

  Thornton, M.M., and R. Devarakonda. 2011. Daymet Single Pixel Extraction Tool.
  ORNL DAAC. https://doi.org/10.3334/ORNLDAAC/2361

Sources disagree on the exact data terms (NASA Earth Science Data and Information Policy,
"full and open sharing"; the AWS Open Data registry lists CC BY 4.0); all ask for the DOI
citation. All Daymet data are provisional and subject to revision.

tests/fixtures/synthetic/opendap_tmax_2020_3x3.nc4 is SYNTHETIC (hand-built by
scripts/make_synthetic_netcdf.py); it is not Daymet data.
